# Security Module - Quick Start Guide

## Installation

```bash
npm install express zod validator isomorphic-dompurify ioredis bcryptjs cookie-parser express-session connect-redis
npm install -D @types/express @types/validator @types/bcryptjs @types/cookie-parser @types/express-session
```

## Basic Setup (2 minutes)

### 1. Environment Variables

Create `.env`:

```bash
NODE_ENV=production
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
SESSION_SECRET=your-secret-here
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com
```

### 2. Initialize Security

```typescript
import express from 'express';
import { productionSecurity } from './security';

const app = express();

app.use(express.json());

// One line to enable all security features
productionSecurity(app, process.env.REDIS_URL);

app.listen(3000);
```

That's it! You now have:
- ✅ Rate limiting
- ✅ CORS protection
- ✅ Security headers
- ✅ CSRF protection
- ✅ Input validation ready

## Common Use Cases

### Protect Authentication Endpoints

```typescript
import { createRateLimiter } from './security';

app.post('/api/auth/login',
  createRateLimiter('auth'), // 5 requests per 15 minutes
  loginHandler
);
```

### Validate User Input

```typescript
import { validateData, signUpSchema } from './security';

app.post('/api/signup', async (req, res) => {
  const result = await validateData(signUpSchema, req.body);

  if (!result.success) {
    return res.status(400).json({ errors: result.errors });
  }

  // Use result.data safely
});
```

### Sanitize HTML Content

```typescript
import { sanitizeHtml } from './security';

app.post('/api/post', (req, res) => {
  const safeContent = sanitizeHtml(req.body.content);
  // Save safeContent to database
});
```

### Protect API with API Keys

```typescript
import { apiKeyAuth, requireScope } from './security';

app.get('/api/data',
  apiKeyAuth(),
  requireScope('data:read'),
  dataHandler
);
```

### Add CSRF to Forms

```ejs
<form method="POST" action="/api/update">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
  <!-- form fields -->
</form>
```

